# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.egg
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- Environment / secrets ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Streamlit's OIDC client secret and cookie secret, for the optional sign-in.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# ---- Data ----
# Raw and derived data are downloaded and rebuilt, never committed. The whole
# corpus is the 39 configured competitions' files from football-data.co.uk,
# re-fetchable in minutes by `make data`, and it changes every match week —
# committing it would be both large and permanently stale.
#
# Nothing under data/ is committed, and no sample slice is either. The
# provider publishes no licence granting redistribution, so this repository
# ships none of its data — see the note in README. The unit suite needs none:
# it runs against synthetic fixtures shaped like the real files, so CI passes
# on a clean checkout with no network. Tests that need real data are marked
# `integration` and skip when it is absent.
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
data/features/*
data/reports/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!data/features/.gitkeep
!data/reports/.gitkeep

# The dashboard's profile store: which leagues and clubs a reader follows,
# written by the dashboard. Local state about a person, not data about
# football, and it is per-deployment rather than per-checkout.
data/dashboard/

# ---- Models ----
models/*
!models/.gitkeep

# ---- MLflow ----
# Experiment tracking state is a local artefact store, not source. The runs
# worth keeping are promoted to the model registry and their metrics written
# into docs/, which is what gets reviewed.
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# ---- Tooling ----
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- Editors / OS / agent tooling ----
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
# Coding agents check a second copy of the tree out here to work in. It is a
# whole duplicate repository inside this one, and it was excluded only by
# .git/info/exclude — which is local to one clone and not something a rule can
# be relied on to survive.
.kilo/
.kilocode/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Local audit and review notes. They are working documents about the
# repository rather than part of it, and the same patterns are in
# .dockerignore so they cannot reach a build context either.
*_AUDIT_REPORT.md
*_PUBLICATION_REPORT.md

# uv.lock is committed on purpose: requirements*.txt pins the direct
# dependencies, and the lockfile pins the transitive closure with hashes, which
# is what makes the benchmark numbers in the README reproducible rather than
# approximately reproducible. Regenerate it with `uv lock` whenever a
# requirements file changes, in the same commit.
#
# poetry.lock stays ignored: nothing here resolves with poetry, and a second,
# unmaintained lockfile in the tree is a source of confusion, not of truth.
poetry.lock
